"Any time of day; taking it every day matters more than when. With a meal is fine." = "Any time of day; taking it every day matters more than when. With a meal is fine.";

/* Evidence card, magnesium: what it is for. */
"Helps muscle and nerve function and energy metabolism. Mainly worth it when your diet falls short." = "Helps muscle and nerve function and energy metabolism. Mainly worth it when your diet falls short.";

/* Evidence card, magnesium: typical dose. */
"Typically 100–250 mg a day from supplements. Citrate and bisglycinate are absorbed well, oxide less so." = "Typically 100–250 mg a day from supplements. Citrate and bisglycinate are absorbed well, oxide less so.";

/* Evidence card, magnesium: timing and food. */
"Often taken in the evening. Large single doses can loosen the stool; splitting them helps." = "Often taken in the evening. Large single doses can loosen the stool; splitting them helps.";

/* Evidence card, vitamin D: what it is for. */
"Supports bones, muscles and the immune system. Matters most in autumn and winter, when the sun in Central Europe is too low." = "Supports bones, muscles and the immune system. Matters most in autumn and winter, when the sun in Central Europe is too low.";

/* Evidence card, vitamin D: typical dose. */
"Commonly 10–50 µg (400–2000 IU) a day. A blood test shows what you actually need." = "Commonly 10–50 µg (400–2000 IU) a day. A blood test shows what you actually need.";

/* Evidence card, vitamin D: timing and food. */
"With a meal that contains some fat, which helps absorption." = "With a meal that contains some fat, which helps absorption.";

/* Evidence card, vitamin C: what it is for. */
"An antioxidant needed for collagen and the immune system. A varied diet with fruit and vegetables usually covers it." = "An antioxidant needed for collagen and the immune system. A varied diet with fruit and vegetables usually covers it.";

/* Evidence card, vitamin C: typical dose. */
"Typically 100–1000 mg a day; most of any excess is excreted." = "Typically 100–1000 mg a day; most of any excess is excreted.";

/* Evidence card, vitamin C: timing and food. */
"Any time. With a meal it helps you absorb iron from plant foods." = "Any time. With a meal it helps you absorb iron from plant foods.";

/* Evidence card, zinc: what it is for. */
"Needed by the immune system, the skin and many enzymes. Endurance athletes and people who eat little meat may run low." = "Needed by the immune system, the skin and many enzymes. Endurance athletes and people who eat little meat may run low.";

/* Evidence card, zinc: typical dose. */
"Typically 5–25 mg a day from supplements." = "Typically 5–25 mg a day from supplements.";

/* Evidence card, zinc: timing and food. */
"Apart from iron and calcium supplements, which compete for absorption. With food if it upsets your stomach." = "Apart from iron and calcium supplements, which compete for absorption. With food if it upsets your stomach.";

/* Evidence card, omega-3: what it is for. */
"Fatty acids from fish or algae that support the heart and brain. Useful if you rarely eat oily fish." = "Fatty acids from fish or algae that support the heart and brain. Useful if you rarely eat oily fish.";

/* Evidence card, omega-3: typical dose. */
"Commonly 250–2000 mg of EPA and DHA combined a day. Count EPA + DHA, not the total amount of oil." = "Commonly 250–2000 mg of EPA and DHA combined a day. Count EPA + DHA, not the total amount of oil.";

/* Evidence card, omega-3 and vitamin K2: timing and food. */
"With a meal that contains fat." = "With a meal that contains fat.";

/* Evidence card, vitamin B12: what it is for. */
"Needed for blood formation and the nervous system. Essential for vegans, because plant foods don't provide it." = "Needed for blood formation and the nervous system. Essential for vegans, because plant foods don't provide it.";

/* Evidence card, vitamin B12: typical dose. */
"Typically 4–1000 µg a day; only a small share of a large dose is absorbed." = "Typically 4–1000 µg a day; only a small share of a large dose is absorbed.";

/* Evidence card: the ingredient can be taken at any time. */
"Any time of day." = "Any time of day.";

/* Evidence card, iron: what it is for. */
"Carries oxygen in the blood. Take it only when a blood test shows low iron: too much is harmful." = "Carries oxygen in the blood. Take it only when a blood test shows low iron: too much is harmful.";

/* Evidence card, iron: typical dose. */
"As advised after a blood test." = "As advised after a blood test.";

/* Evidence card, iron: timing and food. */
"Apart from coffee, tea, calcium and zinc. Vitamin C helps absorption." = "Apart from coffee, tea, calcium and zinc. Vitamin C helps absorption.";

/* Evidence card, selenium: what it is for. */
"Part of antioxidant enzymes and needed by the thyroid. Central European soils contain little of it." = "Part of antioxidant enzymes and needed by the thyroid. Central European soils contain little of it.";

/* Evidence card, selenium: typical dose. */
"Typically 50–200 µg a day. The gap between enough and too much is small." = "Typically 50–200 µg a day. The gap between enough and too much is small.";

/* Evidence card, selenium: timing and food. */
"Any time, with food." = "Any time, with food.";

/* Evidence card, vitamin B6: what it is for. */
"Supports protein metabolism and the nervous system. A normal diet rarely falls short." = "Supports protein metabolism and the nervous system. A normal diet rarely falls short.";

/* Evidence card, vitamin B6: typical dose. */
"Typically 1–10 mg a day; high doses over a long time can harm the nerves." = "Typically 1–10 mg a day; high doses over a long time can harm the nerves.";

/* Evidence card, caffeine: what it is for. */
"Improves alertness and both endurance and strength performance for many people." = "Improves alertness and both endurance and strength performance for many people.";

/* Evidence card, caffeine: typical dose. */
"About 3–6 mg per kg of body weight before exercise (roughly 100–400 mg); smaller doses help too." = "About 3–6 mg per kg of body weight before exercise (roughly 100–400 mg); smaller doses help too.";

/* Evidence card, caffeine: timing and food. */
"30–60 minutes before exercise. Skip the late afternoon and evening if it disturbs your sleep." = "30–60 minutes before exercise. Skip the late afternoon and evening if it disturbs your sleep.";

/* Evidence card, beta-alanine: what it is for. */
"Buffers acid in the muscles and can help in hard efforts of about 1–4 minutes." = "Buffers acid in the muscles and can help in hard efforts of about 1–4 minutes.";

/* Evidence card, beta-alanine: typical dose. */
"3.2–6.4 g a day in split doses, for at least 2–4 weeks." = "3.2–6.4 g a day in split doses, for at least 2–4 weeks.";

/* Evidence card, beta-alanine: timing and food. */
"Split into smaller doses with meals to limit the harmless tingling it can cause." = "Split into smaller doses with meals to limit the harmless tingling it can cause.";

/* Evidence card, sodium: what it is for. */
"The main electrolyte lost in sweat. Replacing it matters in long or hot sessions." = "The main electrolyte lost in sweat. Replacing it matters in long or hot sessions.";

/* Evidence card, sodium: typical dose. */
"Depends on your sweat losses; often 300–1000 mg per hour of long exercise." = "Depends on your sweat losses; often 300–1000 mg per hour of long exercise.";

/* Evidence card, sodium: timing and food. */
"During and after long or hot sessions, with fluids." = "During and after long or hot sessions, with fluids.";

/* Evidence card, potassium: what it is for. */
"An electrolyte for muscle and nerve function. Fruit, vegetables and potatoes are the main sources." = "An electrolyte for muscle and nerve function. Fruit, vegetables and potatoes are the main sources.";

/* Evidence card, potassium: typical dose. */
"Small amounts in electrolyte drinks; large doses from supplements only on medical advice." = "Small amounts in electrolyte drinks; large doses from supplements only on medical advice.";

/* Evidence card, potassium: timing and food. */
"With fluids, during or after exercise." = "With fluids, during or after exercise.";

/* Evidence card, vitamin K2: what it is for. */
"Supports blood clotting and bone health; often combined with vitamin D. If you take blood thinners, ask your doctor first." = "Supports blood clotting and bone health; often combined with vitamin D. If you take blood thinners, ask your doctor first.";

/* Evidence card, vitamin K2: typical dose. */
"Typically 45–200 µg a day." = "Typically 45–200 µg a day.";

/* Evidence card, creatine: note on the limit. */
"No EU upper limit set. EFSA (2004) considers 3 g a day unlikely to pose a risk; studies commonly use 3–5 g." = "No EU upper limit set. EFSA (2004) considers 3 g a day unlikely to pose a risk; studies commonly use 3–5 g.";

/* Evidence card, magnesium: the EFSA limit applies to supplemental magnesium only. */
"Counts magnesium from supplements only (readily dissociable salts and oxide); magnesium in food is not included." = "Counts magnesium from supplements only (readily dissociable salts and oxide); magnesium in food is not included.";

/* Evidence card, vitamin C: no EU limit; the US tolerable upper intake level, labelled as US. */
"No EU upper limit set. The US figure is 2000 mg a day." = "No EU upper limit set. The US figure is 2000 mg a day.";

/* Evidence card, omega-3: note on the limit. */
"No EU upper limit set. EFSA (2012): up to 5 g a day from supplements raises no safety concern." = "No EU upper limit set. EFSA (2012): up to 5 g a day from supplements raises no safety concern.";

/* Evidence card, iron: the 40 mg figure is a safe level, not an upper limit. */
"EFSA's safe level of intake, not a formal upper limit." = "EFSA's safe level of intake, not a formal upper limit.";

/* Evidence card, caffeine: note on the limit. */
"EFSA (2015): up to 400 mg a day, and up to 200 mg at once, raises no safety concern for healthy adults. Coffee counts too, but only what you log here is added up." = "EFSA (2015): up to 400 mg a day, and up to 200 mg at once, raises no safety concern for healthy adults. Coffee counts too, but only what you log here is added up.";

